1
00:00:08,934 --> 00:00:12,662
What's this?

2
00:00:12,662 --> 00:00:13,412
Read it.

3
00:00:13,412 --> 00:00:14,162
I can't.

4
00:00:14,162 --> 00:00:20,204
Would you read it, Marilyn?

5
00:00:20,204 --> 00:00:25,460
"Richard Stewart's show at the Carlson Gallery "Richard Stewaart

6
00:00:25,460 --> 00:00:26,802
is a collection of photographs

7
00:00:26,802 --> 00:00:41,047
from his new book entitled Family Album, U.S.A.

8
00:00:41,047 --> 00:01:16,358
There is power and beauty in Mr. Stewart's work, Stewart

9
00:01:16,358 --> 00:01:22,217
and his book

10
00:01:22,217 --> 00:01:26,761
introduces us to a remarkable new talent."

11
00:01:26,761 --> 00:01:29,339
Oh, Richard, it's wonderful!

12
00:01:29,339 --> 00:01:30,339
Congratulations!

13
00:01:30,339 --> 00:01:38,273
Wow! I'm overwhelmed.

14
00:01:38,273 --> 00:01:39,398
Ladies and gentlemen,

15
00:01:39,398 --> 00:01:44,229
if I may have your attention for a moment, please?

16
00:01:44,229 --> 00:01:47,207
I hope you're all enjoying the exhibition.

17
00:01:47,207 --> 00:01:50,185
I know that I am.

18
00:01:50,185 --> 00:01:52,262
And I would like to introduce the young man

19
00:01:52,262 --> 00:01:54,163
who spent the last five years

20
00:01:54,163 --> 00:01:56,140
taking these remarkable pictures

21
00:01:56,140 --> 00:02:02,096
and writing the background for Family Album,U.S.A.--

22
00:02:02,096 --> 00:02:16,986
Mr. Richard Stewart. Richard Stewarrt

23
00:02:16,986 --> 00:02:17,219
Hello.

24
00:02:17,219 --> 00:02:20,293
I want to thank all of you for coming here tonight.

25
00:02:20,293 --> 00:02:22,266
I'd like to thank Harvey Carlson

26
00:02:22,266 --> 00:02:25,920
for his faith in my project.

27
00:02:25,920 --> 00:02:27,200
But most of all,

28
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:30,398
I would like to thank my family

29
00:02:30,398 --> 00:02:34,854
for their love and support all through this adventure.

30
00:02:34,854 --> 00:02:43,788
Thank you.

31
00:02:43,788 --> 00:02:49,744
Oh, I'm glad that's over.

32
00:02:49,744 --> 00:02:51,744
Would you mind?

33
00:02:51,744 --> 00:03:04,634
Oh, not at all.

34
00:03:04,634 --> 00:03:04,930
Thanks.

35
00:03:04,930 --> 00:03:05,522
Our pleasure.

36
00:03:05,522 --> 00:03:07,298
Hope it wins a Pulitzer Prize.

37
00:03:07,298 --> 00:03:16,545
I'll settle for an "A" in my photography course.

38
00:03:16,545 --> 00:03:19,523
Ah, Richard, Marilyn, I want you to meet John O'Neill.

39
00:03:19,523 --> 00:03:21,203
Oh, how do you do?

40
00:03:21,203 --> 00:03:22,501
Nice to meet you.

41
00:03:22,501 --> 00:03:25,479
I've been looking forward to meeting your husband, Mrs. Stewart.

42
00:03:25,479 --> 00:03:28,457
I'm really impressed by your show.

43
00:03:28,457 --> 00:03:29,207
Thank you.

44
00:03:29,207 --> 00:03:31,435
In fact, I'd like your autograph.

45
00:03:31,435 --> 00:03:32,935
Oh, well, really ...

46
00:03:32,935 --> 00:03:34,413
On a contract.

47
00:03:34,413 --> 00:03:37,391
What's this about, Harvey?

48
00:03:37,391 --> 00:03:40,869
Mr. O'Neill is the publisher of several magazines. O'Neill

49
00:03:40,869 --> 00:03:45,187
Of course. I've seen you on television.

50
00:03:45,187 --> 00:03:47,272
Mr. O'Neill was so impressed with your work O'Neill

51
00:03:47,272 --> 00:03:51,843
that he wants to develop it into a magazine concept.

52
00:03:51,843 --> 00:03:53,567
Well, that sounds very exciting,

53
00:03:53,567 --> 00:03:56,259
but where would I fit into the plan?

54
00:03:56,259 --> 00:03:59,237
I'd like you to be the photo editor of the magazine.

55
00:03:59,237 --> 00:04:01,215
Oh, Richard, how exciting!

56
00:04:01,215 --> 00:04:04,193
It's a wonderful opportunity, Richard.

57
00:04:04,193 --> 00:04:08,931
Hold on. Wait a minute, please.

58
00:04:08,931 --> 00:04:10,149
What's the problem, Richard?

59
00:04:10,149 --> 00:04:16,105
The problem is that I'm a photographer, not an editor.

60
00:04:16,105 --> 00:04:17,105
I like what I do.

61
00:04:17,105 --> 00:04:19,083
In fact, I love what I do ...

62
00:04:19,083 --> 00:04:23,110
which is going out with a camera and a roll of film

63
00:04:23,110 --> 00:04:25,413
and seeing the wonder of humanity.

64
00:04:25,413 --> 00:04:27,288
Now, I appreciate your offer,

65
00:04:27,288 --> 00:04:33,099
but I've worked so hard on Family Album, U.S.A.,

66
00:04:33,099 --> 00:04:57,796
and I'm giving some thought to a new book on a different subject.

67
00:04:57,796 --> 00:05:01,274
I'm flattered,

68
00:05:01,274 --> 00:05:45,443
but I enjoy taking pictures, and I want to continue doing that.

69
00:05:45,443 --> 00:05:46,443
Thank you,

70
00:05:46,443 --> 00:06:45,003
but I'm happy being a photographer.

71
00:06:45,003 --> 00:06:48,313
I understand, Richard.

72
00:06:48,313 --> 00:06:53,208
Richard, I know your next book will be a success. Richard

73
00:06:53,208 --> 00:07:14,782
Congratulations!

74
00:07:14,782 --> 00:07:16,282
Thanks.

75
00:07:16,282 --> 00:07:18,360
You're a real Stewart!

76
00:07:18,360 --> 00:07:21,360
Thanks.
